Shared State Binding

Cards can bind directly to shared state:

```lua
Window:CreateState("project_name", "Crystal Core", {Persist = true})

Main:CreateInput({
    Id = "project_name_input",
    Title = "Project Name",
    Default = Window:GetState("project_name"),
    State = {
        Name = "project_name",
        Persist = true,
    },
    Persist = true,
})
```

State binding forms:
- `State = "project_name"`
- `State = { Name = "project_name", Persist = true }`
- `BindState = "project_name"`

Computed State

```lua
Window:CreateComputedState(
    "summary",
    {"project_name", "density"},
    function(get)
        return string.format("%s | %.2f", get("project_name") or "Untitled", tonumber(get("density") or 0))
    end
)
```

Use computed state for:
- summary labels
- status text
- search-facing derived strings
- rules that need a stable shared read model

Persistence

The persistence layer is now first-class and should be finished before more major card growth.

What gets persisted when opted in:
- theme
- custom theme color
- blur intensity
- open field of view
- toggle/minimize/theme-cycle keys
- holder position
- active tab
- shared state where `Persist = true`
- cards where `Persist = true`

Recommended persistence pattern:
- use shared state for business/UI intent
- set `Persist = true` on cards that should restore directly
- expose `SaveConfiguration`, `LoadConfiguration`, `ExportConfiguration`, and `ImportConfiguration` through one visible panel

Preset helper:
- `Window:CreateSettingsPanel(target, cfg)`
  Builds profile input, import/export buffer, settings access, save/load/export/import buttons, and search focus.

Notifications, Modals, and Search

`Window:SendNotification({
    Title = "...",
    Subtitle = "...",
    Duration = 3,
    JumpTo = {Tab = "Main", Id = "some_card"},
    Queue = "stack" | "replace",
    MaxVisible = 4,
    Actions = {
        {Label = "View", JumpTo = {Tab = "Main", Id = "some_card"}},
        {Label = "Retry", Callback = function() end},
    },
})`

Supported notification concepts:
- action buttons
- jump-to-card/tab behavior
- queue replacement
- max visible stack count
- notification history via the action center

Search notes:
- search now matches card title
- subtitle
- id / flag / card id
- tab name
- recent queries are tracked internally

